From: Luissalet <luismasc16@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 00:49:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/36] Pin the sd-server request surface and the PNG metadata
 round trip

The payload test asserts the whole object, not a field at a time: a plain
request must still serialise exactly as it did, so nothing new can drift
into it by accident. Every new key is checked against the name the
server's parser reads, and checked to be absent when nobody asked for it.

The PNG tests build their fixture with their own CRC-32 so a bug in the
module cannot bless itself, and cover the cases that matter in practice:
a non-Latin-1 prompt, a rewrite, a truncated file and a chunk claiming
more bytes than the file holds.

